-- title:
--   Package fibre dictionary and centre-pinned model read equal places
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak P$ be a level-$N_0q$ Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose residue field $\kappa_A$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ be a ring map from $\mathbb Z_{(q)}=\{x\in\mathbb Q:\gcd(\mathrm{den}(x),q)=1\}$ to $\kappa_A$. Let $M_s$ be a curve model over $\kappa_A$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa_A\,N_0$, the subfield of $\kappa_A((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\kappa_A\,d\,(j\bmod q)$ for $d\mid N_0$, and let $e_s$ be an isomorphism from $M_s.C$ onto the base change of Igusa's scheme $\mathrm{igusaTo}\,N_0\,q$ along $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$, compatible with the structure maps ($e_s$ followed by the second projection is $M_s.\mathrm{toBase}$). Let $fm$ be a fibre model `FibreModel N₀ A q κ_A (residue A)`, assumed (hypothesis `hfin`) to have its subring $fm.BFin$ containing the coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{coeffEmb}$ of every element of the finite chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,N_0\,q$ (the $\mathbb Z_{(q)}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,N_0$ of elements integral over $\mathbb Z_{(q)}[j]$). The centre-pinning hypothesis `hspFin` requires: for every $\kappa_A$-point $y$ of $M_s$ (a section of $M_s.\mathrm{toBase}$) and every ring map $\beta$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,N_0\,q$ to $\kappa_A$ such that $y$ followed by $e_s$ and the first projection equals $\mathrm{Spec}(\beta)$ followed by the finite-chart inclusion $\mathrm{\iota Fin}\,N_0\,q$, and for every $b$ in that chart algebra, the element $fm.\mathrm{piFin}(b)$, viewed in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa_A\,N_0$ along $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\le\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}$, lies in the valuation subring of the place $M_s.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,y$ and differs from the constant $\beta(b)$ by a nonunit of that subring. Finally $hCF$ asserts the equality of intermediate fields $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_A\,N_0=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa_A\,N_0$. The conclusion: for every $\kappa_A$-point $y'$ of the package's fibre curve model $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{Mfib}\,\kappa_A\,\mathrm{to}\kappa$ (a curve model over $\kappa_A$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_A\,N_0$), the place attached by $M_s$ to the $\kappa_A$-point $y'$ followed by $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{efib}$ and by $e_s^{-1}$ coincides with the transport, under $\mathrm{Place.congrRingEquiv}$ along the ring isomorphism induced by $hCF$ (comap of the valuation subring along its inverse), of the place attached by $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{Mfib}\,\kappa_A\,\mathrm{to}\kappa$ to $y'$.
--
--   This is the comparison of the two dictionaries for the special fibre of $X_0(N_0q)$ at $q$: the one carried by a Deligne–Rapoport model package through `Mfib` and `efib`, and any model of the full fibre field identified with the base change of Igusa's scheme and pinned at the centres of the finite chart. It is used in the analysis of the crossing points of that special fibre, by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.base_closedPoint_eq_crossing_of_reduceFst_eq_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.base_closedPoint_eq_crossing_of_reduceFst_eq_of_sp_eq_spPlace), [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.compat_reduceFst_reduceSnd_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.compat_reduceFst_reduceSnd_of_sp_eq_spPlace) and [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.section_base_closedPoint_eq_crossing_of_reduceFst_mem_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.section_base_closedPoint_eq_crossing_of_reduceFst_mem_of_sp_eq_spPlace).
